package cajeta.net.uri;

/**
 * Selects which **component-specific safe set** percent-encoding uses
 * (plan item **NET-6.2**).
 *
 * RFC 3986 does *not* have one universal "encode everything that isn't
 * unreserved" rule — each component permits a different subset of the
 * **reserved** characters to appear *un*-encoded, because the delimiter
 * that would otherwise terminate the component differs per component.
 * Encoding too aggressively is lossy round-trip-wise; encoding too
 * little corrupts the structure. So the encoder is parameterized by the
 * component it is producing.
 *
 * ## The safe sets (RFC 3986 §2.3 + §3)
 *
 * Every component keeps the **unreserved** set raw:
 *
 * ```
 * unreserved = ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "." / "_" / "~"
 * ```
 *
 * On top of that, each component additionally permits some of the
 * **sub-delims** and a couple of **gen-delims**, per its ABNF:
 *
 * ```
 * sub-delims = "!" / "$" / "&" / "'" / "(" / ")"
 *            / "*" / "+" / "," / ";" / "="
 * pchar      = unreserved / pct-encoded / sub-delims / ":" / "@"
 * segment    = *pchar
 * query      = *( pchar / "/" / "?" )
 * fragment   = *( pchar / "/" / "?" )
 * userinfo   = *( unreserved / pct-encoded / sub-delims / ":" )
 * reg-name   = *( unreserved / pct-encoded / sub-delims )
 * ```
 *
 * The ordinal values below are **stable** — [`PercentCodec`](PercentCodec.cajeta)
 * switches on them to pick the safe-set predicate. Don't reorder
 * without updating that map.
 *
 *   - `PATH`     — a whole path: `pchar` plus the `/` segment separator
 *                  is left raw (a path *containing* slashes is normal).
 *   - `SEGMENT`  — a single path segment: `pchar`, but `/` **is**
 *                  encoded (so an embedded slash can't split the
 *                  segment — the form `Uri.percentEncode` callers use
 *                  when injecting one untrusted segment).
 *   - `QUERY`    — `pchar` plus `/` and `?` raw. (A query-*value* with a
 *                  literal `&` or `=` should use `QUERY_PARAM`.)
 *   - `QUERY_PARAM` — a single key or value within a query: like
 *                  `QUERY` but `&`, `=`, `+`, `;` are encoded so they
 *                  can't be read as separators by the NET-6.3 parser.
 *   - `FRAGMENT` — identical safe set to `QUERY` (`pchar` / `/` / `?`).
 *   - `USERINFO` — `unreserved` / sub-delims / `:`.
 *   - `HOST`     — reg-name: `unreserved` / sub-delims (no `:` or `@`).
 */
public enum UriComponent {
    PATH,
    SEGMENT,
    QUERY,
    QUERY_PARAM,
    FRAGMENT,
    USERINFO,
    HOST
}
